{"name":"Garden Twilight","hex":"#a3bbb3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"},{"term":"twilight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft light in the sky seen before the rising and (especially) after the setting of the sun, occasioned by the illumination of the earth’s atmosphere by the direct rays of the sun and their reflection on the earth.","The time when said light is visible; the period between daylight and darkness."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to or resembling twilight; faintly illuminated; obscure.","Synonym of mesopelagic (“Describing the pelagic zone of the ocean between the photic epipelagic and the aphotic bathypelagic zones, characterized by very minimal light.”)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twilight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"},{"title":"Twilight","blocks":[{"text":"Twilight is daylight illumination produced by diffuse sky radiation when the Sun is below the horizon as sunlight from the upper atmosphere is scattered in a way that illuminates both the Earth's lower atmosphere and also the Earth's surface. Twilight also may be any period when this illumination occurs, including dawn and dusk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Twilight_description_full_day.svg/330px-Twilight_description_full_day.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilight","wikidata":"Q164160"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/1280px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Skylands3.jpg/500px-Skylands3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The New Jersey Botanical Garden at Skylands Estate","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASkylands3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG/500px-%27JardimBotanico.BotanicalGarden.CuritibaParanaBrasilBrazil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Partial view from the Botanical Garden of Curitiba (Southern Brazil): parterres, flowers, fountains, sculptures, greenhouses and tracks composes the place used for recreation and to study and protect t